  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::3745",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine appears to interact with multiple potassium channel subunits through a shared mechanism of binding to delayed rectifier potassium channels, as evidenced by its interaction with Kcna6, Kcnv2, and Kcna7, all of which participate in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. This suggests that Guanidine may modulate potassium channel function by targeting these subunits, potentially influencing the activity of Kcnb1, a subunit of the delayed rectifier potassium channel. The consistent involvement of these channels in the same biological process implies a functional link between Guanidine and Kcnb1, likely through a common pathway involving potassium channel regulation. The evidence supports a mechanism where Guanidine exerts its effects by interacting with potassium channels, which in turn modulate Kcnb1's activity, though the exact molecular details of this interaction remain to be elucidated.",
